  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building of Grassroots Organizations for Community Management of Water Resources &amp; Nature</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As part of the Programme seeking to address issues of water contamination and scarcity in the Altoplano, the Platform for Climate Change  will aim to build the capacity of indigenous communities associated to CONAMAQ, ANARESCAPYS, CORIDUP and other grassroots and social organizations. In doing so, the Platform for Climate Change seeks to transfer tools that will improve water management practices at a local level, as well as generate solid advocacy processes that will reduce the vulnerability of the population to climate change. By identifying positive community practices that respond to contamination and climate change issues, the Climate Change Platform will foster exchanges and the sharing of lessons learned to disseminate information and promote the replica of successful experiences. This project will also foster the creation of a pilot water sub-basin management committee that will give the Platform&apos;s members a better understanding of how national legislation and advocacy can be applied in a real life situation.</narrative>
  </description>
